  "company_description": "Flex Ltd. provides technology innovation, supply chain, and manufacturing solutions to data center, communications, enterprise, consumer, automotive, healthcare, industrial, and power industries in the Americas, Asia, and Europe. The company operates through three segments: Integrated Technology Solutions (ITS), Regulated Manufacturing Solutions (RMS), and Cloud and Power Infrastructure (CPI). The ITS segment offers flexible supply and manufacturing solutions for communications, including high speed networking, enterprise, and satellite communications systems, as well as lifestyle solutions comprising products across commercial, home, and personal product categories. Its RMS segment includes industrial products, such as mission critical automation, energy, and industrial infrastructure; automotive products, including compute and power electronics platforms and integrated systems; and healthcare products comprising regulated manufacturing for medical devices, drug delivery, and equipment. The CPI segment provides cloud and cooling products, such as integrated compute systems supporting power dense digital infrastructure deployments and advanced liquid cooling solutions supporting higher density, power intensive rack architectures; and power products that include utility and facility level electrical infrastructure enabling power delivery and high density rack and board level power systems. The company was formerly known as Flextronics International Ltd. and changed its name to Flex Ltd. in September 2016. Flex Ltd. was founded in 1969 and is headquartered in Austin, Texas.",
  "company_description_source": "data-lake/FLEX/10K/FLEX_2026-05-20.htm.gz -> Item 1 Business, Overview / Business Overview",
  "ai_positioning": {
    "stance": "integrator",
    "summary": "Flex ne developpe pas de modeles ou puces IA mais integre les infrastructures physiques (alimentation electrique, refroidissement, systemes de calcul) qui equipent les centres de donnees IA de ses clients, via son segment Cloud and Power Infrastructure (CPI) desormais en cours de scission.",
    "evidence": [
      "Rapport annuel de l exercice 2026 (Item 1, Business) : Flex \"support[s] the design, manufacture, and lifecycle management of a range of power, thermal, and compute infrastructure products used for AI data centers and mission-critical applications\", avec des capacites en produits d'alimentation critique, refroidissement et infrastructure de calcul en rack.",
      "Le chiffre d'affaires du segment CPI est passe de 3,244 Mds $ (12% du CA, FY2024) a 4,799 Mds $ (19%, FY2025) puis 6,614 Mds $ (24%, FY2026), une trajectoire de croissance directement liee a la demande en infrastructure de centres de donnees (Rapport annuel de l exercice 2026, note segments).",
